---
import { siteConfig } from "../../config";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <title>Propel Case Study | Pamela Yung</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A UX case study redesigning Propel into a benefits and grocery planning tool."
    />
  </head>

  <body class="bg-white text-gray-900">
    <Header />

    <main>
      <!-- HERO -->
      <section class="min-h-screen p-8 sm:p-12 md:p-16 lg:p-24 flex items-center">
        <div class="w-full">
          <a
            href="/"
            class="inline-block text-sm sm:text-base font-mono text-gray-600 hover:text-gray-900 transition"
          >
            ← Back to Home
          </a>

          <div class="mt-20 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-16 items-start">
            <div class="lg:col-span-12">
              <p
                class="text-sm sm:text-base font-mono mb-6"
                style={`color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}
              >
                UX CASE STUDY / PRODUCT DESIGN / FIGMA
              </p>

              <h1 class="text-5xl sm:text-6xl md:text-7xl xl:text-8xl font-bold leading-[0.95] tracking-tight text-gray-900">
                Propel Benefits
                <br />
                <span style={`color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}>
                  & Grocery Planning
                </span>
                <br />
                Redesign
              </h1>

              <p class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-xl sm:text-2xl font-mono leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
                I redesigned Propel into a benefits and grocery planning tool that helps users track EBT balance,
                monitor grocery inventory, reduce food waste, and make more informed spending decisions.
              </p>

              <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                <span class="px-3 py-1.5 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-lg text-sm font-medium">Figma</span>
                <span class="px-3 py-1.5 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-lg text-sm font-medium">UX Research</span>
                <span class="px-3 py-1.5 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-lg text-sm font-medium">Product Design</span>
                <span class="px-3 py-1.5 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-lg text-sm font-medium">User Flows</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- HERO IMAGE -->
      <section class="p-8 sm:p-12 md:p-16 lg:p-24 pt-0">
        <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-4 sm:p-6 shadow-sm">
          <img
            src="/images/propel/hero.png"
            alt="Propel app redesign screens"
            class="w-full rounded-xl border border-gray-200"
          />
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- OVERVIEW -->
      <section class="p-8 sm:p-12 md:p-16 lg:p-24">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-16 items-start">
          <div class="lg:col-span-4">
            <p class="text-sm font-mono" style={`color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}>01</p>
            <h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-gray-900">
              Overview
            </h2>
            <div
              class="w-[75px] h-[5px] mt-4 rounded-full"
              style={`background-color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}
            />
          </div>

          <div class="lg:col-span-8">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
              <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-mono leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
                Propel helps users manage benefits-related information, including EBT balance tracking and support resources.
                For this redesign, I focused on connecting benefits, grocery inventory, and budgeting so users could make
                clearer decisions around food and spending.
              </p>

              <p class="mt-6 text-lg sm:text-xl font-mono leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
                My role included contributing to user research, identifying user needs, mapping user flows, and creating
                high-fidelity prototype screens that communicate the redesigned experience.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- PROBLEM -->
      <section class="p-8 sm:p-12 md:p-16 lg:p-24">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-16 items-start">
          <div class="lg:col-span-4">
            <p class="text-sm font-mono" style={`color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}>02</p>
            <h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-gray-900">
              Problem
            </h2>
            <div
              class="w-[75px] h-[5px] mt-4 rounded-full"
              style={`background-color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}
            />
          </div>

          <div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-6">
            <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-mono leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
              People who rely on EBT benefits often need to make careful decisions around grocery spending,
              food inventory, and upcoming deposits. However, checking a balance alone does not always help users
              understand what they already have at home, what food may expire soon, or how to plan purchases around
              their remaining benefits.
            </p>

            <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
              <p class="text-xl sm:text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold leading-relaxed">
                How might we help Propel users connect their benefits, grocery inventory, and spending habits so they can make more informed food and budgeting decisions?
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- USER RESEARCH -->
      <section class="p-8 sm:p-12 md:p-16 lg:p-24">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-16 items-start">
          <div class="lg:col-span-4">
            <p class="text-sm font-mono" style={`color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}>03</p>
            <h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-gray-900">
              User Research
            </h2>
            <div
              class="w-[75px] h-[5px] mt-4 rounded-full"
              style={`background-color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}
            />
          </div>

          <div class="lg:col-span-8">
            <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-mono leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
              Our research showed that users need more than a balance number. They need to understand what food they
              already have, what may expire soon, when their next deposit is coming, and how their spending affects
              future grocery decisions.
            </p>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mt-10">
              <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
                <p class="text-sm font-mono" style={`color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}>INSIGHT 01</p>
                <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Quick access matters</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 font-mono leading-relaxed">
                  Users need balance, deposit, and spending information upfront.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
                <p class="text-sm font-mono" style={`color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}>INSIGHT 02</p>
                <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Food planning is connected</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 font-mono leading-relaxed">
                  Grocery inventory and benefits planning should not feel separate.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
                <p class="text-sm font-mono" style={`color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}>INSIGHT 03</p>
                <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Reminders reduce waste</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 font-mono leading-relaxed">
                  Expiration and quantity prompts help users use what they already have.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- USER FLOWS -->
      <section class="p-8 sm:p-12 md:p-16 lg:p-24">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-16 items-start">
          <div class="lg:col-span-4">
            <p class="text-sm font-mono" style={`color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}>04</p>
            <h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-gray-900">
              User Flows
            </h2>
            <div
              class="w-[75px] h-[5px] mt-4 rounded-full"
              style={`background-color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}
            />
          </div>

          <div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-8">
            <figure class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-4 sm:p-6">
              <img
                src="/images/propel/user-flow-1.png"
                alt="Propel user flow 1"
                class="w-full rounded-xl border border-gray-200"
              />
              <figcaption class="mt-4 text-sm font-mono text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                User Flow 1 maps how users move from checking benefit status to finding relevant support.
              </figcaption>
            </figure>

            <figure class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-4 sm:p-6">
              <img
                src="/images/propel/user-flow-2.png"
                alt="Propel user flow 2"
                class="w-full rounded-xl border border-gray-200"
              />
              <figcaption class="mt-4 text-sm font-mono text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                User Flow 2 maps how users discover grocery savings, inventory tools, and planning features.
              </figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- DESIGN DIRECTION -->
      <section class="p-8 sm:p-12 md:p-16 lg:p-24">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-16 items-start">
          <div class="lg:col-span-4">
            <p class="text-sm font-mono" style={`color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}>05</p>
            <h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-gray-900">
              Design Direction
            </h2>
            <div
              class="w-[75px] h-[5px] mt-4 rounded-full"
              style={`background-color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}
            />
          </div>

          <div class="lg:col-span-8">
            <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-mono leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
              I wanted the visual design to feel clear, friendly, and supportive. Since the app deals with financial
              benefits and food access, the interface needed to feel trustworthy without feeling cold or overly formal.
            </p>

            <div class="mt-10 bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-4 sm:p-6">
              <img
                src="/images/propel/style-guide.png"
                alt="Propel design system"
                class="w-full rounded-xl border border-gray-200"
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- FINAL PROTOTYPE -->
      <section class="p-8 sm:p-12 md:p-16 lg:p-24">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-16 items-start">
          <div class="lg:col-span-4">
            <p class="text-sm font-mono" style={`color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}>06</p>
            <h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-gray-900">
              Final Prototype
            </h2>
            <div
              class="w-[75px] h-[5px] mt-4 rounded-full"
              style={`background-color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}
            />
          </div>

          <div class="lg:col-span-8">
            <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-mono leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
              The final prototype focuses on three connected areas: benefits tracking, grocery inventory,
              and budgeting support.
            </p>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mt-10">
              <figure class="group bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-white hover:shadow-xl hover:border-gray-300 hover:-translate-y-1">
                <img
                  src="/images/propel/home-dashboard.png"
                  alt="Propel home dashboard"
                  class="mx-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200"
                />
                <figcaption class="mt-5 text-sm font-mono text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                  The home dashboard gives users a quick view of their EBT balance, recent spending, next deposit timeline, and grocery reminders.
                </figcaption>
              </figure>

              <figure class="group bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-white hover:shadow-xl hover:border-gray-300 hover:-translate-y-1">
                <img
                  src="/images/propel/spending-breakdown-chart.png"
                  alt="Propel spending breakdown"
                  class="mx-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200"
                />
                <figcaption class="mt-5 text-sm font-mono text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                  The spending breakdown helps users understand where their benefits are going across stores and categories.
                </figcaption>
              </figure>

              <figure class="group bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-white hover:shadow-xl hover:border-gray-300 hover:-translate-y-1">
                <img
                  src="/images/propel/inventory-overview.png"
                  alt="Propel inventory overview"
                  class="mx-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200"
                />
                <figcaption class="mt-5 text-sm font-mono text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                  The inventory overview helps users track what food they already have at home and what should be used soon.
                </figcaption>
              </figure>

              <figure class="group bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-white hover:shadow-xl hover:border-gray-300 hover:-translate-y-1">
                <img
                  src="/images/propel/grocery-planner.png"
                  alt="Propel grocery planner"
                  class="mx-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200"
                />
                <figcaption class="mt-5 text-sm font-mono text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                  The grocery planner supports future shopping decisions by connecting planned purchases with inventory and price information.
                </figcaption>
              </figure>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- REFLECTION -->
      <section class="p-8 sm:p-12 md:p-16 lg:p-24">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-16 items-start">
          <div class="lg:col-span-4">
            <p class="text-sm font-mono" style={`color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}>07</p>
            <h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-gray-900">
              Reflection
            </h2>
            <div
              class="w-[75px] h-[5px] mt-4 rounded-full"
              style={`background-color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}
            />
          </div>

          <div class="lg:col-span-8">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
              <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-mono leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
                This project helped me think more intentionally about how product design can reduce cognitive load.
                Benefits information can easily become overwhelming, so I focused on designing screens that help users
                quickly understand what matters and what they can do next.
              </p>

              <p class="mt-6 text-lg sm:text-xl font-mono leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
                If I continued this project, I would test the prototype with users to understand whether the dashboard,
                grocery inventory, and budgeting tools feel clear and useful in real situations.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>